  body: "# Gainful employment in the non-income-related earnings chapter\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\
    \nThe captured chapter describes gainful employment through a desire, hope or intention of remuneration,
    or actual payment regardless of that intention, for the non-income-related benefit contexts it lists.\n\
    \n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 15000 expressly excludes UC, JSA, IS, ESA and Pension Credit from
    this chapter’s earnings rules. Its Incapacity Benefit, Carer’s Allowance and dependency-increase uses
    have their own conditions and historical boundaries. This is not a universal employment or tax-status
    definition.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 15000, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n- [DMG 15010, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n- [DMG 15011, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a04ed307d7bff3604d6dc3/dmgch15.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 3: Ch 15: Earnings for non-income-related benefits.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\n\
    Model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot.
    Specialist review is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this
    record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted
    text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage
    or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch15`: PDF SHA-256 `b9a278572b8205196c4b0c2d1b0c3c8032dddff62587e3ba0ff7fc897c670e4e`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `37d8db04ba2cd204591b67e3f3d8099a4c96be8f86ee788c70ab275322060a70`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/common-unknown-versus-unreceived-earnings
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter distinguishes estimating earnings whose amount is unknown from treating
      unreceived earnings as possessed; the gainful-employment meaning does not collapse those
      cases.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0005
      quote: "15014 Where it is not possible to find out what the claimant’s earnings are at the time
        the DM is making\nthe decision, the claimant is treated as having such earnings as is reasonable
        in the circumstances taking\n\ninto account the number of hours worked and the earnings paid for
        comparable employment in the area 1.\n\n\n                                                   \
        \                        1 SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg 4(1)\n\n\n\n\nNo earnings or earnings less
        than for comparable employment"
      locator: DMG 15014
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0005
      quote: "15015 On 11.11.02 a Commissioner decided1 that the regulation2 which permits a DM to take
        into account\nnotional earnings where a person is working for nothing or for less than that paid
        for comparable\nemployment in the area was ultra vires.\n\n\n                                \
        \                              1 R(IB) 7/03; 2 SS Ben (C of E) Regs, reg 4(2)"
      locator: DMG 15015
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch15/0005
      quote: "15016 This means that, in these circumstances, a claimant cannot be treated as possessing
        earnings\nwhich that person does not in fact possess. As the notional earnings provisions are
        not available DMs\nshould consider the NMW Provisions. See DMG 15017 - 15019.\n\n\n\n\nNational
        minimum wage"
      locator: DMG 15016
